7-bd0983f12961" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533964 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186533159 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533964 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186533428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533964 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186533578 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533964 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186533632 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533964 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533964 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533964 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186533159 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533964 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f8b3efd3-b7c3-58e8-b4b9-9e7263c863ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533984 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186533773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533984 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186533806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533984 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186533896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533984 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186533964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533984 #edb/ref 1069 "q-336094" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533984 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533984 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$ is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are linearly independent for all $t$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $det(Φ(t))\\ne 0$ for all $t$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ introduces the notation for the {{field-1}} of {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from line {{field-4}} by the properties of determinants." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533984 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "20281150-3bf1-5302-a5be-765695a3b8d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533984 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first interpret line $\\text{L1}.$ Line $\\text{L1}$ introduces the notation for the $\\text{columns}$ of $Φ,$ namely the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$ These functions are the fundamental solutions of the system.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of the solution space for our system. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Recall that a matrix has linearly independent columns if and only if its determinant is nonzero. Since ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are linearly independent for any particular $t,$\n\n$$\ndet(Φ(t))\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by the properties of determinants." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534093 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186533801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534093 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186533851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534093 #edb/ref 1069 "q-334388" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534093 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534093 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">${e}^{6t}-{e}^{-6t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">${e}^{6t}-{e}^{-6t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr></tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534093 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f69ba2b0-76ef-5087-a5bf-906e0adf24a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534093 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & 6{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 6{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-6t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=6t,\n$$\n\neach of multiplicity one. Thus, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}r(-6t)={e}^{-6t} \\\\ r(6t)={e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-6t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-6t} \\\\ 6t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- Subtracting the second equation from the first one, we get\n\n$$\n-12t{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-6t}-{e}^{6t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{1}=-\\frac{1}{12t}({e}^{-6t}-{e}^{6t}).\n$$\n\n- Adding the first and the second equations, we get\n\n$$\n2{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-6t}+{e}^{6t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-6t}+{e}^{6t}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-6t}+{e}^{6t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{6t}+{e}^{-6t}) \\\\ 6{\\alpha }_{1}t & =6\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{12t}({e}^{-6t}-{e}^{6t}))t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{6t}-{e}^{-6t})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{6t}+{e}^{-6t} & {e}^{6t}-{e}^{-6t} \\\\ {e}^{6t}-{e}^{-6t} & {e}^{6t}+{e}^{-6t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534109 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "231eb329-513b-5dfb-85da-6e0f13afe8fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534109 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186533984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534111 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186534142 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534111 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "24523b4e-4e57-53cd-8b40-7f56c7c2589e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534111 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186398781 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534127 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186534111 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534127 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "62363ed1-22ab-56fa-9971-8c017f526c79" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534127 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186221991 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534128 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186534109 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534128 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6372c740-c40b-54b4-b2d8-d67db30bf1d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534128 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186365673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534142 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186534128 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534142 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a9bd7aaf-ed47-5adf-8e37-bc1f645e1959" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534142 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186534093 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
